            <div xml:id="d856">

                <pb facs="0856" n="852" sameAs="frus:frus1939v03/pg852"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.51 Salt Funds/237a: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Ambassador in
                        China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Johnson</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1939-08-12T15:00:00-04:00">August 12, 1939—3
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>156. Reference your 367, June 9, 9 a.m. and Shanghai’s despatch no. 2291, June
                    23, 1939,<anchor n="94" xml:id="d856-f1"/> in regard to foreign personnel of the
                    Chinese Government Salt Administration.</p>
                <p>Having in mind the considerable holdings by American citizens of financial
                    obligations secured on the Chinese Government salt revenues, the Department
                    desires your comment (<hi rendition="#italic">a</hi>) on any progress made in,
                    and possible effects of, the proposed completion of merger of the Salt
                    Administration with the Ministry of Finance and (<hi rendition="#italic">b</hi>)
                    on the question of the advisability of an informal approach by you to the
                    Chinese Minister of Finance in regard to the more effective employment of the
                    foreign staff of the Salt Administration and in regard to betterment of service
                    conditions affecting the foreign staff.</p>
                <p>Sent to Chungking. Repeated to Peiping and Shanghai.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Welles</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
